  "pages": 20
 },
 "summary": "Optically isolated relays that switch AC loads on 100 V or 200 V rms lines with one normally open triac output blocking 600 V. An LED input driven at 15 to 25 mA fires a phototriac, which in turn fires a power triac; the isolation is 5,000 V rms. Three current grades (0.3, 0.9 and 1.2 A rms) come in zero-cross and random-fire versions, each in through-hole DIP or surface-mount form. AQH2223 is the 0.9 A random-fire part in through-hole DIP, packed in tubes.",
